																		Site Criticism Team - Review
															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rockteethmotheyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4022320); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4022320&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238168" alt="RockTeethMothEyes" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4022320)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rockteethmotheyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4022320); return false;" >RockTeethMothEyes</a></span> <span class="odate time_1574734539 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">26 Nov 2019 02:15</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4431702">
									

<p>Noting for transparency that the most I did for this in the draft stages was find a license compliant image (source is <a href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/24736216@N07/4975852892">here</a>, by the way) and some minor help with questions brought up in the IRC chatrooms. Overall, this did not do much to impress.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+[Critique]&nbsp;Click&nbsp;to&nbsp;Access</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-[Click&nbsp;to&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Text]</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>This doesn't really go to a place that I find satisfying. One could very much reach the implication that the oranges are dying while in containment, but as for <em>why</em> that is or why the Foundation doesn't pick up on it isn't clear. It almost comes off as incompetent, but not quite.</p>
<p>My primary issue with the article is that a lot of time is spent detailing the behavior of the oranges and their traits. I think that they pray for the dead is very interesting. I think that the tree secretes glucose is a nice touch. However, these things can easily be omitted as they don't support the narrative of the article. Similarly, the table of tests isn't doing much to carry the article either, as it's stuff that could easily be summarized in the description, in my opinion (I am wondering how the Foundation had the foresight to include a metal cage in one of the tests if their intent was to test for the -2's response to live fauna). The weirdness is incredibly tame and not nearly enough.</p>
<p>The build up to the ending does not feel sufficient. I'd even go as far to say that the pacing is a flat line throughout, not really spiking in tension or dread. For me, this didn't feel like it went anywhere.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><span style="font-size:smaller;"><strong>Disclaimer:</strong> <em>Opinions expressed in this review do not reflect the opinions of SCP Wiki staff as a whole. Please respond to <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rockteethmotheyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4022320); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=4022320&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1574734539" alt="RockTeethMothEyes" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=4022320)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rockteethmotheyes" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(4022320); return false;">RockTeethMothEyes</a></span> or contact the captain of the Site Criticism Team, <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=637830&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1574734539" alt="SoullessSingularity" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=637830)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/soullesssingularity" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(637830); return false;">SoullessSingularity</a></span>, for any questions or concerns relating to this review.</em></span></p>

