				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1404533&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238168" alt="Zyn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1404533)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/zyn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1404533); return false;" >Zyn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1574832620 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Nov 2019 05:30</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4432756">
									

<p>Porting my forum crit over:</p>
<p>Right from the start, some of the wording could use some changing for better flow/straightforward reading. For example:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>SCP-XXXX-1 is to be misted for one hour daily with fresh, distilled water, and requires at least 7 hours per day of either artificial or natural sunlight. &gt; &quot;SCP-XXXX-1 requires at least 7 hours of artificial or natural sunlight per day, and is to be misted daily with fresh distilled water for one hour.&quot;</li>
<li>The classification of SCP-XXXX is applicable to two different entities: &gt; &quot;SCP-XXXX is the collective designation for the following anomalies:&quot;</li>
</ul>
<p>Also some general formatting/nitpicks:</p>
<ul>
<li>Personnel Level 1 or higher &gt; &quot;Personnel with Level-1 clearance or higher&quot;</li>
<li>Plant seeds are to be provided to SCP-XXXX-2 in order to keep instances content. &gt; what kind of plant seeds? Just any plant seeds? Fruit-specific? Fertile seeds? Any kind of seeds? I personally feel like the Foundation would just keep a designated cache for this anomaly.</li>
<li>similarly to ones found in humans &gt; I would use &quot;those&quot; and not &quot;ones&quot;</li>
<li>&quot;The average height for an SCP-XXXX-2 instance is 2.34 meters tall.&quot; &gt; no need for &quot;tall&quot; since you already mention it's height being measured.</li>
<li>SCP-XXXX-2 instances are gradually produced from SCP-XXXX-1. SCP-XXXX-1 appears to self-regulate the amount of SCP-XXXX-2 instances, maintaining a population that does not exceed 17 at any given time. &gt; you can combine these sentences.</li>
<li>One (1) packet &gt; Generally, the number (#) numeration is used for extreme precision measurements that can be fatal if misinterpreted, like drug prescriptions. Alternatively, it's for legal reasons to avoid ambiguity. You don't need to do that with easy to count whole numbers.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>Overall, I felt like at the end of the article I found myself asking, &quot;so what?&quot; These are little orange entities that do typical human things, but the list of behaviors they exhibit get a little predictable after awhile (the table of reactions seem to amount to &quot;they like this&quot; and &quot;they don't like this&quot;, most of which the audience could probably figure out themselves if asked) and the ending of &quot;suddenly they're sad and dying out&quot; feels abrupt. It almost feels kind of underhanded that the ending is just the little orange dudes suddenly starting to do poorly, especially since there isn't really any buildup to why they're doing badly (except hanging out near the entrance? Why didn't the Foundation react accordingly and move them to an open-air aviary or something? (Although, I'm surprised that the Foundation moved the tree to a greenhouse instead of containing it where it was found. Transplanting fruit trees can be tricky business.)</p>
<p>My suggestions:</p>
<ul>
<li>develop the &quot;culture&quot; of these orange entities more. Make them more distinct from humans somehow. Maybe they pray by releasing citric acid scents into the air. Maybe they domesticate bugs.</li>
<li>add some more background as to what these things actually are in the context of the Foundation universe. Spirits of farmers who worked in orange orchards? The helpers of some citrus fruit deity, like the <a href="/scp-3243">Green Warden</a>'s mushroom buddies? Something else entirely?</li>
<li>don't end the piece on a hamfisted sad note. Give the audience a bit of hope so they don't feel like the story was a letdown. Have the Foundation figure out what's going wrong, change the containment accordingly, and have the last note be about the Foundation stating that the population recovery is a tentative success.</li>
</ul>
<p>Novote from me since I believe this could be much better, but I don't necessarily think it's downvote-worthy as it is.</p>

