															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/diamonddorsal" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3052156); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3052156&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608238169" alt="DiamondDorsal" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3052156)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/diamonddorsal" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3052156); return false;" >DiamondDorsal</a></span> <span class="odate time_1574929297 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">28 Nov 2019 08:21</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4433635">
									

<p>I don't know why but I find my self drawn to this SCP, which has prevented me from straight up down voting it, however I do still have some problems with this SCP:</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Issues&nbsp;and&nbsp;Critique</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;And&nbsp;Possible&nbsp;Soloutions</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<ul>
<li>I see what you trying to do by showing that how the Foundation does not know how to properly contain this SCP, and while it doesn't come off as lolfoundation, it still feels a bit too obvious for most people that their doing something wrong, and can come of as overly incompetent (especially for a foundation that specialises in the containment of the anomalous), which ruins the immersion of the reader.
<ul>
<li>The foundation should begin to recognise a decreasing population quickly, and perhaps dedicate some test logs in which they try to find out why and how the population is decreasing. It doesn't matter if they succeed or not, but the chance that they could save them is all that is needed to keep the narrative engaging, speaking of which&#8230;</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>The description focuses a bit too much on the oranges and can make it difficult to transition to the the main narrative (which I'm assuming is related to the extinction of SCP-4021). I get the feeling you were perhaps trying to get the reader to become emotionally attached which can be an effective tool for keeping them engaged, however it slows down the pace and can make the transition feel rough
<ul>
<li>Shorten the description a bit and put more focus on the part in which the SCP is slowly dying off.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>In short, this SCP has potential, and despite its flaws I grew still fond of these mandarins, but please address these issues since I do not think many people will be as kind. Novote for now.</p>

							</div>

								
					
